  "caseStudy": {
    "title": {
      "en": "Adrenal crisis after missed stress-dose steroids",
      "zh": "漏用应激剂量激素后的肾上腺危象"
    },
    "summary": {
      "en": "A client with known adrenal insufficiency cannot tolerate oral steroids during illness and develops shock, hypoglycemia, and electrolyte abnormalities.",
      "zh": "已知肾上腺功能不全患者患病期间无法耐受口服激素，进展为休克、低血糖和电解质异常。"
    },
    "exhibits": [
      {
        "id": "adrenal_initial",
        "title": {
          "en": "Urgent care presentation",
          "zh": "急诊初始表现"
        },
        "content": {
          "en": "A 59-year-old client with autoimmune adrenal insufficiency arrives with vomiting, weakness, abdominal pain, and dizziness after a febrile gastroenteritis illness. The client states, 'I could not keep my hydrocortisone pills down for two days.' Vital signs: T 101.1 °F (38.4 °C), HR 122/min, RR 24/min, BP 84/46 mm Hg. Skin is cool and mottled.",
          "zh": "59岁自身免疫性肾上腺功能不全患者因发热性胃肠炎后呕吐、无力、腹痛和头晕来诊。患者说：“这两天氢化可的松片吃了就吐。”生命体征：T 101.1 °F (38.4 °C)，HR 122次/分，RR 24次/分，BP 84/46 mm Hg。皮肤发凉并呈花斑。"
        }
